DCTFilter r3.2 (HomeOfVapourSynthEvolution/VapourSynth-DCTFilter, tag r3.2 =
45bc72a): upstream's own thread-safety fix, commit c924a7a ("Remove locks, use
vsh_aligned_malloc", 2026-05-10), which no tag contains yet (VapourBox task
#96, docs/reports/task-96-dctfilter-thread-race).

The filter is fmParallel and kept one 64-float scratch buffer per worker
thread in an std::unordered_map on the filter instance. Up to r2.1 (what the
Windows and macOS x64 bundles shipped) the map was filled from getFrame with
no lock at all; r3.0-r3.2 lock the insert and the lookup but still call
count() outside the lock. Two threads starting their first frame together
corrupt the map or lose an insert, and the lookup's .at() then throws
std::out_of_range inside a noexcept function: std::terminate, so vspipe
aborts ("unordered_map::at: key not found"; on Windows the UCRT's abort is a
fail-fast, exit 0xC0000409). Measured with r2: about 1 vspipe run in 100.

c924a7a drops the map: each getFrame allocates its own 64-byte-aligned
buffer and frees it, and the planning buffer is aligned the same way, which
FFTW's new-array execute requires. The output is unchanged (same plans, same
arithmetic). Planning stays FFTW_PATIENT, as upstream has it.

Applied by download-deps-{macos,linux}.sh and download-deps-windows.ps1 right
after the clone; each build fails if it stops applying.

